  "implementation_approach": "{\"phases\":[{\"phase\":\"Phase 1\",\"description\":\"Harness, matcher, google clients and constants (PRs 1-2)\",\"deliverables\":[\"lib/michael/feeder.mjs + test\",\"lib/michael/rules-match.mjs + test\",\"lib/michael/google-clients.mjs + test\",\"gmail-client.mjs read methods\",\"lib/michael/constants.mjs + test\",\"quiet-tick imports the shared window helpers\"]},{\"phase\":\"Phase 2\",\"description\":\"Host feeders (PRs 3, 4a, 4b, 5)\",\"deliverables\":[\"calendar-read.mjs + test\",\"gmail-triage.mjs read-only + test\",\"gmail-triage --apply with ceiling + tests\",\"tasks-classifier.mjs + test\"]},{\"phase\":\"Phase 3\",\"description\":\"GHA feeder, host registrar, seat verbs (PRs 6-8)\",\"deliverables\":[\"todoist-brief.mjs + workflow + wiring test\",\"setup-michael-host-tasks.mjs + wrappers + test + measured schtasks result\",\"queue-read.mjs, classify-apply.mjs + tests, role-contract tick paragraph\"]}],\"technical_decisions\":[\"michael-family feeder shape with the window gate in the harness (VALIDATION condition 3)\",\"brief-assemble and its workflow belong to child E; -D exports only the pure ordering predicate (condition 2)\",\"retention is superseded by child B (condition 1)\",\"gmail-triage split at the read/write boundary so the read-only half merges while the ceiling is under review (condition 5)\",\"No per-item metering; the seat feeder_runs row carries model_used/tokens (finding 3)\",\"tasks-classifier stages the cleanup list instead of writing to Drive: the grant is drive.readonly in v1\",\"Task Scheduler /SC MINUTE all day with in-script windows; wake-from-sleep documented, not configured\",\"No DDL in this child\"]}",
